Riftway Chromium patch 0012: elastic overscroll only for a renderer with --scroll-bounce.

macOS pages rubber-band when scrolled past their ends because the renderer
reports elastic overscroll as supported (RenderThreadImpl::
IsElasticOverscrollSupported, IsElasticOverscrollEnabledOnRoot). Electron
turns it off unless webPreferences.scrollBounce is set, which adds
--scroll-bounce to the renderer's command line: both now answer whether the
renderer's own command line has the switch, as Electron's
scroll_bounce_flag.patch does. Riftway adds the switch through CEF patch 0010
for the renderers of a session created with SessionOptions.ScrollBounce.
No CEF API change.

Resolves: Riftway docs/DRIFT.md W55 (with 0010).
Base: Chromium 154.0.8037.94 with CEF a03e714's patches. Applies in chromium/src.
diff --git a/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc b/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc
index a884b89..206da24 100644
--- a/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc
+++ b/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc
@@ -1193,11 +1193,11 @@ bool RenderThreadImpl::IsLcdTextEnabled() {
 }
 
 bool RenderThreadImpl::IsElasticOverscrollEnabledOnRoot() {
-  return is_elastic_overscroll_enabled_on_root_;
+  return base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch("scroll-bounce");
 }
 
 bool RenderThreadImpl::IsElasticOverscrollSupported() {
-  return is_elastic_overscroll_supported_;
+  return base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch("scroll-bounce");
 }
 
 blink::scheduler::WebThreadScheduler*
